  "answer_text": "The address **`www.home.fedex.com/express`** (or simply `home.fedex.com`) is the URL for the **internal FedEx employee intranet portal** (specifically the FedEx Express homepage). \n\n### Crucial Security Restriction\nIf you are currently trying to open this link from home or on a personal device, **it will not load**. \n\nBecause this is a secure internal intranet site, it is protected by the FedEx corporate firewall. **It can only be accessed while you are connected to the physical FedEx network**\u2014meaning you must be on-site at a FedEx hub, station, or office, and using a company-authorized work computer. \n\n---\n\n### How to Access FedEx Employee Info From Home\nIf you are off the clock and trying to access your pay stubs, benefits, or schedules, you must use external-facing web portals rather than the internal intranet:\n\n1. **For General Apps & Password Resets:**\n   * You can use the secure external portal: **`myapps.secure.fedex.com`**. \n   * You will need your **Purple ID** and password to log in. (Note: Multi-factor authentication via text, call, or authenticator app is usually required to log in from a home device).\n2. **For Pay Stubs & Payroll:**\n   * **Express and Freight employees** can log into the **iFedEx HR portal** or the *FedEx My Payroll* system to view earnings and print W-2s.\n   * **Ground employees** typically use **Workday** to manage schedules and view payroll.\n3. **Checking Hours Worked (Dimensions):**\n   * Most stations restrict access to *Dimensions* (the time-tracking software) to the internal network. If you need to verify your hours or make a correction and cannot wait until your next shift, you will need to contact your manager directly to have them check for you.",
